## summary
D=18 (9-fold): 18/19/40/100/176/327/663/1218 = 2,561 tilings to k=8. 12.6 s single core (contended
with the D=24 pool, so the figure is an upper bound). k7->k8 ratio 1.84, down from 2.03 at k6->k7.
Raw blocks 7555; face filter keeps 331 of 3839 vertex types.

D=20 (5-fold): 6/0/0/0/0/0/0/0 = 6 tilings, ALL 1-uniform. k=8 RUN, not assumed: 7 raw blocks, 0
survive above k=1. D=20 is now confirmed empty at every k from 2 to 8. Face filter keeps 49 of 1667.

Out-of-ring records reaching the atlas at k=8: 9fold 22 (up from 6 at k=7 — the biggest jump in the
series), 5fold 0. The 9fold export keeps only blocks carrying a tile whose symmetry order does not
divide 24; the other 1196 k=8 D=18 tilings are alpha-samples of in-ring families and belong to the
star24full shelf, not here.
